{"name":"Belle of the Ball","hex":"#e3cbc0","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"belle of the ball","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The woman who is the most beautiful or attractive at a dance or similar function"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/belle_of_the_ball"}],"entries":[{"title":"Belle of the Ball","blocks":[{"text":"Belle of the Ball is a 2023 lesbian romance graphic novel by Mari Costa."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Belle_of_the_Ball"},{"title":"Belle (Disney character)","blocks":[{"text":"Belle is a fictional character in Disney's Beauty and the Beast franchise. First appearing in the 1991 animated film, Belle is the book-loving daughter of an inventor who yearns for adventure and respite from her mundane village. When her father is imprisoned by a cold-hearted beast, Belle offers her own freedom in exchange for his. Despite his outward appearance, she gradually befriends the Beast, who learns kindness in return."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/d/d5/Belle_disney.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Belle_(Disney_character)"},{"title":"Ball","blocks":[{"text":"A ball is a round object. Balls can have several uses. For example they are used in ball games, where the play of the game follows the state of the ball as it is hit, kicked or thrown by players. Balls can also be used for simpler activities, such as catch or juggling. Balls made from hard-wearing materials are used in engineering applications to provide very low friction bearings, known as ball bearings. Black-powder weapons use stone and metal balls as projectiles."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ce/Many_balls.jpg/330px-Many_balls.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ball"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/44/Katharine_hepburn_little_women.jpg/330px-Katharine_hepburn_little_women.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/44/Katharine_hepburn_little_women.jpg/330px-Katharine_hepburn_little_women.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Screenwriter Linda Woolverton based Belle on actress Katherine Hepburn's performance in Little Women (1933).","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AKatharine_hepburn_little_women.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d5/Paige_O%27Hara_%2849200407146%29.jpg/500px-Paige_O%27Hara_%2849200407146%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d5/Paige_O%27Hara_%2849200407146%29.jpg/500px-Paige_O%27Hara_%2849200407146%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Belle's voice actress, Paige O'Hara.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APaige_O'Hara_(49200407146).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b6/Vivien_Leigh_Scarlet.jpg/500px-Vivien_Leigh_Scarlet.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b6/Vivien_Leigh_Scarlet.jpg/1280px-Vivien_Leigh_Scarlet.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b6/Vivien_Leigh_Scarlet.jpg/500px-Vivien_Leigh_Scarlet.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"British actress Vivien Leigh was one of several classical Hollywood actresses who inspired Belle's physical appearance.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AVivien_Leigh_Scarlet.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d9/Anneliesevande